While I was browsing the source for poisoning arrows another idea
occured to me: Why are only weapons poisonable? Surely the more
natural idea is to poison food? What if you could apply potions of
sickness, sleep, paralysis, or confusion to food and somehow offer it
to monsters?

Of course, currently the only monsters that eat anything, as far as I
know, are tame pets, wild domestic animals which you have thrown food
to (and why would you want to poison a prospective pet?) or gelatinous
cubes. So the whole area of monsters eating food would have to be
dealt with.

And I guess that's not such a good idea, as you certainly wouldn't
want monsters eating all the food on a level before you can get to it.
But surely there is some way of making this work? The poisoned apple
is such a strong folkloric symbol, it deserves to be somewhere in
nethack.

Any ideas?

